From eee23a17ffe14089e4aa2bf93ca1103394c5bdb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] radv: add a PS4 winsys

-Dradv-winsys=ps4 builds RADV for the PS4's Liverpool GPU (GFX7,
described as a Bonaire):

- buffers are direct memory mapped at the same address for the CPU and
  the GPU, with a reserved window for 32-bit pointers, and are freed
  once the submissions using them have finished;
- command streams are copied into a ring and submitted as DCBs with
  sceGnmSubmitCommandBuffers, ending with an EOP that writes a sequence
  number to a completion marker;
- the shader cache defaults to /data/radv-shader-cache.

There is no Vulkan loader on the PS4, so RADV is built as libvulkan.so.1
and exports the Vulkan API itself (vk_exports_gen.py), with a vulkan.pc.
The build needs -Dradv-build-id, since there is no dl_iterate_phdr.

Co-authored-by: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
